tic cancer model  pancos2 where you don't see a complete  response but you definitely see a much  better partial response with the leptin  expressing virus um compared to the  virus control  when we're looking at the tumor  infiltrating lymphocytes we also see  that these tumors have a much better  functional t cell infiltration where you  can see that they're expressing much  more  uh cytokines in terms of tnf alpha and  in the pheno gamma compared to the  control virus  they're also producing they're also  generating  a lot more mitochondrial mass and this  is observed by the staining of vdac  you're seeing a lot more vdac a higher  percentage of vdac in the leptin  expressing virus tumors compared to  their controls and uh importantly too we  are actually observing an increase in uh  proliferative capacity in these t cells  as well where we see a higher percentage  of ti-67 staining  in the t cells from the  tumors  treated with the leptin vaccinia tumor  vaccinia virus  and so just to look a little bit further  at the populations that are in in the  tumor  after treatment and looking specifically  at the populations in terms of like the  t cell clusters we can divide the t  cells that are infiltrating into these  tumors after treatment in different  populations such as memory cytotoxic  c4t cells t-rex um exhausted and one of  the things that it was highlighted  during the analysis was that there was  an increase in general of the memory  population  and so when we did uh till analysis we  did see that the tumors that were  treated with the vaccine leptin have an  increase  in cd127 expressing tumor t cells  showing that in general there's a um and  a skewing towards a memory population  which would be also beneficial for  better uh response to the immunotherapy  so doing immediate so trying to see if  this memory activity is true  what we did was a memory experiment  where  we had a cohort of mice that got treated  with the vaccinia leptin expressing  virus  as