u a little bit of a  uh  brief uh data that we have that is uh  preliminary  um like i mentioned before i talked  about how foxb3 cd4  positive t cells  population decrease after  vaccinia treatment so that we found it  was very interesting that in a way we're  targeting the tear eggs which is good  and in the terms of like a tumor setting  and so in collaboration with um  with the hink lab here in pittsburgh who  develops  these pgf beta uh inhibitors he produced  a tga beta mini monomer which is  basically a com  a monomer that binds to the pj beta r2  receptor in  in this way it out competes a tga beta  and that way there's no um there's no tn  beta downstream signaling so what we  initially did was  treat cells with the vaccinia virus and  get  the supernatant from vaccinia control as  well as the vaccine  that had the tgf beta monomer and what  you see here in the graph when you just  have the control vaccinia plus cg of  beta you have a higher tissue beta  activity  when you include the supernatant from  the uh the cells that were treated with  the vaccinia tj beta virus you can see a  decrease in tgf-b activity in this  activity gets diluted as the supernatant  gets diluted as well showing that it's  specific for tj beta activity  and most importantly when we  look at the tumor growth with these with  this virus you actually do see an  improvement in treatment compared to the  vaccine control with the tgf beta  virus and so this is just the  preliminary data that we've been  developing in the lab and we're further  exploring um  in in with different um  compounds and so just to give a overall  summary for my talk  uh  vaccinia can be utilized to induce an  immune response in cold tumors pretty  efficiently um in this immune response  needs uh some metabolic support to be  able to function better  and  most importantly vaccinia viruses as  well as other oncolytics can ha can be  genetically modified to provide that  metabolic support  and so i just wanted to give a quick  acknowledgement for my lab um my lab  that i'm in with  my mentor greg delgov and everyone in  the lab and of course my collaborators  at pitt that have been instrumental for  this project to move forward and with  that um i'm done and if anybody has any  questions  in the future please contact me i'll be  happy to answer any questions you guys  have thank you
 

